  "answer": "The supplied Manual gives two separate procedures. The requirements below are Manual practice; the relevant provisions of the Act and Regulations are referred to by the Manual but are not themselves supplied.\n\n1. Splitting off goods — divisional application\n• Lodge a divisional application identifying the goods to be divided out and specifying the goods/services to remain in the parent. It must cover ‘some only’ of the parent’s goods/services, use the same trade mark and applicant, and be divided from a single parent application. [TMM/Part12/3#1]\n• File while the parent is still pending and while the goods being divided out are still in its specification. Do not delete those goods first. If deletion submissions also state that a divisional will be filed, the Manual says to delay deletion until that filing. ‘Pending’ includes accepted and opposed applications. [TMM/Part12/2#1; TMM/Part12/x-annex-a1-divisional-checklist-for-divisional-applications-filed-on-or-after-27-march-2007#1]\n• Avoid duplication between the divisional goods and those specified to remain in the parent. The Manual generally requires restrictions to remove duplication, if possible, or deletion of the reference to the divisional priority date. Once the divisional is valid and complete without duplication, the examiner processes the parent’s amendment as soon as practicable. [TMM/Part12/x-annex-a1-divisional-checklist-for-divisional-applications-filed-on-or-after-27-march-2007#1]\n\n2. Late costs filing — extension of time\n• For a late application for an award of costs or a bill of costs filed outside the reg 21.12 time limit, lodge an extension-of-time application in the approved form, together with the appropriate fee and a supporting declaration. The Manual says the late costs filing can only be considered if an extension under s 224 is granted; lodging the extension request alone is not enough. [TMM/Part55/3/3/4]\n• If the extension sought exceeds three months, the extension application must be published for opposition purposes. [TMM/Part55/3/3/4]\n\nTiming limitation: the supplied costs passage does not state the ordinary reg 21.12 deadline or a specific deadline for lodging the extension request. I therefore cannot give an exact costs lodgement date from these passages. Nor are ss 45–46, s 224 or regs 21.12 and 21.25 supplied for direct legislative verification."
